@startuml preserve-rebuild
!pragma layout smetana
!include ../_includes/theme.puml

title Preserve versus rebuild: where each mode runs and where Remote Control sits

node "Node (one OS user)" as NODE {
  component "Session host\nsupervisor + journal" as HOST $SERVICE

  rectangle "Preserve mode" as PRES {
    component "Holder\nowns the PTY" as HP $SERVICE
    component "Native TUI\n(Claude, Codex, Muse)" as TUI $AGENT
    file "Native resume\n(--resume UUID,\nthread/resume)" as NR $PRIVATE
  }

  rectangle "Rebuild mode" as REB {
    component "Holder\nowns framed pipes" as HR $SERVICE
    component "Structured surface\n(stream-json, app-server, MSP)" as ST $SERVICE
    file "Versioned handoff\n(export + seed)" as VH $COMMITTED
    component "New execution\n(fresh execution refs,\nseeded conversation)" as NX $SERVICE
    file "Linkage\n(old → new, at H)" as LK $COMMITTED
  }

  rectangle "Operator compatibility" as RC {
    component "Claude Remote Control\n(vendor-authenticated\nparallel channel)" as RCH $AGENT
  }
}

HOST --> HP : typed writes,\nreadiness-checked paste
HP --> TUI : owns the terminal
TUI --> NR : harness-owned continuity
HOST --> HR : typed writes
HR --> ST : framed protocol
ST --> VH : export at H
HOST --> NX : fresh admitted launch
VH --> NX : seed only\nauthorized content
NX --> LK : record linkage
RCH --> TUI : parallel input\n(no session-core envelope)

note right of VH
  Rebuild is handoff, export, seed.
  A journal states its supported
  fidelity; it preserves no hidden
  model or native tool state.
  Native resume and seeded
  conversation are distinct.
end note

note right of RCH
  Outside per-message assurance.
  Strict (mode S) sessions refuse RC
  across all enablement routes.
  Unavailable per-input provenance
  is recorded as unknown.
end note

note bottom of HOST
  Mode T gates managed bridge input.
  Mode S additionally requires
  demonstrated isolation at launch
  and resume; without it the S
  request is refused or parked,
  never silently run as T.
end note

caption Sources: Architecture v1 §A3, §A4; session-core study rev 3 (modes T/S, RC classification)
@enduml
